{red|**If you are the unfaithful spouse, honestly assess where you are in this process.**

Have you completely terminated contact with the affair partner?}{red| Have you offered radical transparency?}{red| Are you demonstrating patient endurance or are you pushing for faster healing?}

{red|What aspects of this work are you struggling with?}{red| What excuses or justifications are you still holding onto?}

Write your honest assessment:

{red|**Reflect on how disclosure has been handled in your situation.**

If you are the betrayed spouse, do you feel you have the full truth?}{red| Are there questions you still need answered?}{red| Has there been trickle truth?}

{red|If you are the unfaithful spouse, have you disclosed everything?}{red| Are you still hiding anything?}

{red|What needs to happen with disclosure for you to move forward?}

Write your reflection:

{red|**You do not have to have a final answer, but it can be helpful to acknowledge where you are leaning right now.**

What factors are making you consider staying?}{red| What factors are making you consider leaving?}

{red|What would need to be true for you to choose to stay and work on this marriage?}{red| What would need to be true for you to choose to leave?}

Write your honest reflection:

{red|If you are the betrayed spouse, what boundaries would help you feel safer?}

{red|If you are the unfaithful spouse, what boundaries are you willing to accept?}{red| Is there anything you are resisting, and if so, why?}

{red|What boundaries are already in place?}{red| What is missing?}

Write your reflection:

{red|If you are the betrayed spouse, what are your main triggers?}{red| What brings the pain flooding back?}{red| What do you typically need when triggered?}

{red|If you are the unfaithful spouse, how have you been responding when your spouse is triggered?}{red| What could you do differently?}

Write your reflection:

{red|**This week, discuss triggers and create a plan for handling them together.**

**Identify the main triggers.** Can any be avoided?}{red| If not, how will you handle them when they occur?}

{red|**Discuss what the betrayed spouse needs during a trigger.** Words?}{red| Presence?}{red| Space?}{red| Physical comfort?}

**Create a phrase or signal that means I am triggered right now to allow quick communication without having to explain.**

**Having a plan does not make triggers painless, but it helps you navigate them as partners rather than having them drive you apart.**

Write your trigger plan:

{red|**Honestly assess where you are in the forgiveness journey.**

Are you still acknowledging the wound and grieving?}{red| Have you made a choice to forgive?}{red| Do you find yourself choosing forgiveness repeatedly as anger resurfaces?}

{red|What would help you move forward?}

Write your honest reflection:

{red|**Reflect on where you are with sexual intimacy since the affair.**

If you are the betrayed spouse, what are you feeling about physical intimacy?}{red| What triggers exist?}{red| What do you need from your spouse?}

{red|If you are the unfaithful spouse, how have you been handling this aspect of recovery?}{red| Have you been patient and sensitive?}

Write your reflection:

{red|**Have an honest conversation about sexual intimacy in your recovery.**

**Discuss where you each are emotionally with physical intimacy.** What feels safe?}{red| What does not?}

{red|**Discuss specific triggers.** Are there acts, times, or contexts that are particularly difficult?}

{red|**Discuss what you each need.** More patience?}{red| More communication?}{red| More initiative?}{red| Less pressure?}

{red|**This conversation may feel awkward.** Have it anyway. The alternative is two people guessing and potentially hurting each other.

What do you need to communicate about sexual intimacy?}

{red|If you are choosing to rebuild, what do you want the new marriage to look like?}

{red|What was missing from the old marriage that needs to be present in the new one?}{red| What patterns need to change?}{red| What kind of couple do you want to become?}

